# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the Python-driven leg of the sanitizer lane
# (.github/workflows/sanitizers.yml, pytest-asan job).
#
# Entries match function names anywhere in an allocation's stack. These two
# cover CPython's own allocator machinery, whose arenas and interned objects
# legitimately survive pytest at process exit on interpreter builds where
# pymalloc falls back to intercepted malloc. kith allocations never pass
# through those functions (they allocate directly inside libkith_*.so), so
# framework findings stay visible.
#
# Known masking boundary: a Python-object leak allocated on behalf of kith
# code (the worker pool dispatching Python handlers) carries _PyObject*
# frames and is suppressed by the patterns below; leaks of that shape need
# triage outside this lane.
leak:_PyObject*
leak:*obmalloc*
